  "id": "vagus-nerve",
  "term": "vagus nerve",
  "definition": "The vagus nerve is the tenth cranial nerve. It carries incoming sensory information from part of the outer ear and from organs in the throat, chest, and abdomen, and it also sends parasympathetic and voluntary motor signals to structures in the throat, chest, and abdomen.",
